# pico-dgx-ds4 — copy to .env and edit (start.sh/stop.sh load ./.env;
# .env itself is gitignored): cp .env.example .env
# Tensor parallelism. The engine kernels/ring are TP=4 specialised today,
# so anything != 4 is cut-planned (dsw_convert --world $TP) but refused by
# dsgb10_rank until the kernels are generalised. Keep 4 for serving.
TP=4
# Fleet file. Either the repo's reference (edit a copy) or one generated from
# TP: WORKERS="user@spark1 user@spark2 user@spark3" ./start.sh fleet
FLEET=./ds41f-4xgx10-switchless/fleet/homelab.conf
# ssh targets of ranks 1..TP-1, used by ./start.sh fleet. Rank 0 is the head
# and runs locally, so the count is TP-1: 3 for TP=4, 1 for TP=2. WORKER= is
# an alias when there is exactly one.
# WORKERS="olyno@10.0.0.4 olyno@10.0.0.3 olyno@10.0.0.2"   # TP=4
# WORKERS="olyno@10.0.0.4"                                  # TP=2
# ./start.sh fleet knobs: LINK_BASE (192.168.LINK_BASE.0/24, 2 subnets a link),
# GID_INDEX, NEXT_DEV0/1, PREV_DEV0/1; any RANK<r>_* value set here wins.
# LINK_BASE=10
# Prepare: `./start.sh` runs it by itself, and only when a rank's files are not
# already where the fleet says. It looks for the checkpoint in
# ~/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017, ~/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, /data/models/* and the Hub
# cache before downloading anything; the artefacts go to the directory the fleet
# puts rank 0's weight file in (RANK0_WEIGHTS), the revision is pinned in the
# tool, and the space needed is computed from the plan. It streams the checkpoint
# as it converts (--consume, and at --cpu-shares 512 so the rest of the box keeps
# its CPU), resumes an interrupted run, and leaves finished ranks alone. To keep
# the checkpoint, run `./start.sh prepare` without --consume first: it refuses if
# the copy cannot fit rather than deleting it.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...        # only for a gated or private checkpoint
# The checkpoint is Xet-backed and needs xet (the image ships hf_xet); HF_NO_XET=1
# forces the classic path, which the Hub refuses for files this large.
# HF_NO_XET=1
# Served endpoint.
DSGB10_PORT=18893
DSGB10_ADDR=127.0.0.1
# API key file (created by start.sh if missing; mode 600).
DSGB10_KEY_FILE=$HOME/dsgb10-data/dev-api-key
# 1: no bearer key at all (dsfront runs without --api-key-file); only safe on
# loopback or a trusted network. The key file is then neither created nor read.
# DSGB10_NO_AUTH=1
# Images: VISION=1 keeps the encoder's slice of the checkpoint (~2.3 GB: its
# inference/ scripts plus the shards holding vision./aligner./image_ tensors)
# during prepare, and points dsfront at 127.0.0.1:18950. VISION_IMAGE names a
# torch/PIL/safetensors image; start.sh runs tools/vision/vision_encoder.py from it
# against that bundle. VISION=0 (default) refuses image parts, as before.
# VISION=0
# VISION_IMAGE=<image with torch + PIL + safetensors>
# Confidence-gate weights. start.sh deploys the repo's copy here (once), then
# service.sh copies it to ranks 1..TP-1. If neither this path nor the repo copy
# exists, the server still runs on the shipped confidence head: slower drafts,
# the same tokens.
DSGB10_CF_MLP=$HOME/cfmlp_cml.bin
# Engine / front-end arguments (defaults in start.sh are the production ones).
# DSGB10_ENGINE_ARGS="--max-ctx 262144"
# DSGB10_FRONT_ARGS="--tokenizer $HOME/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash/tokenizer.json --model-name deepseek-v4.1-flash"
# Direct ring: 2 only when every rank reaches every other in one hop, i.e. all
# TP boxes on one switch (this repo's fleet: yes; +1-2 % with the same bits).
# Leave unset on a cabled ring, and on a 2-box link — there rank r's opposite
# would be itself, so there is nothing to write directly.
# DSGB10_RING_DIRECT=2
# Container.
IMAGE=pico-dgx-ds4:latest
SKIP_BUILD=0
WAIT_TIMEOUT=900
# DRY_RUN=1
